Subject: [PATCH] wireguard: accept UDP tunnel GSO before software segmentation

WireGuard's transmit entrypoint segments GSO skbs before encryption, but
its feature mask omits UDP tunnel GSO. Transmit validation therefore
segments VXLAN traffic before wg_xmit, making each resulting packet a
separate staged/crypto queue submission and defeating encrypted batching.

Advertise both UDP tunnel GSO variants in the existing feature mask.
wg_xmit still performs complete software segmentation with zero offload
features before admitting records for encryption. This changes neither
the wire format nor per-record authentication, checksums or ordering.

The source-level VXLAN fixture covers both WireGuard endpoint families,
IPv4/IPv6 VXLAN underlays and TCP payloads, IPv4 UDP checksum modes, and
both directions. Its batching assertion rejects the previous feature mask.
Physical throughput and the signed Talos/DRBD lifecycle are separate gates.

---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireguard/device.c b/drivers/net/wireguard/device.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireguard/device.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireguard/device.c
@@ -276,7 +276,9 @@
 	struct wg_device *wg = netdev_priv(dev);
 	enum { WG_NETDEV_FEATURES = NETIF_F_HW_CSUM | NETIF_F_RXCSUM |
 				    NETIF_F_SG | NETIF_F_GSO |
-				    NETIF_F_GSO_SOFTWARE | NETIF_F_HIGHDMA };
+				    NETIF_F_GSO_SOFTWARE | NETIF_F_HIGHDMA |
+				    NETIF_F_GSO_UDP_TUNNEL |
+				    NETIF_F_GSO_UDP_TUNNEL_CSUM };
 	const int overhead = MESSAGE_MINIMUM_LENGTH + sizeof(struct udphdr) +
 			     max(sizeof(struct ipv6hdr), sizeof(struct iphdr));
 
